// Dead-range stand-aside: record that the market is too quiet to trade, so a
// host can suppress entry rules, without proposing a position or halting
// anything. ATR_PCTL_INV(120) = 100 minus the percentile rank of ATR(14)/close
// within its own trailing 120 bars, so 100 is the quietest bar of that history.
// RANGE_QUIET_COUNT = how many of the 10-, 20- and 50-bar high-low ranges sit in
// the bottom quintile of their own 120-bar history (0 to 3). Both are published
// as complements because narrower is the condition of interest and baseline IR
// cannot carry a negative literal.
// REGIME: compression with no catalyst - the stretch where most entry rules are
// trading noise. Do NOT read it as a forecast of a breakout; it says nothing
// about direction or timing.
// CONDITIONS: ATR in the quietest tenth of its own recent history AND all three
// range windows agreeing. Three windows agreeing is the point: a single window
// can be pinched by one holiday bar or a data gap, three cannot all be.
// INVALIDATION: any window leaving its bottom quintile, or ATR rising out of the
// quietest tenth. No latch; the host decides what suppressing entries means.
// SHAPE: 1h; a flat, coiled tape where every timeframe looks the same.
// NOT bb_squeeze_breakout: that enters long on one absolute band width plus
// momentum and bets the squeeze breaks. This proposes no position, measures
// against the instrument's own history so it travels, and needs three windows
// to agree. NOT squeeze_release_expansion: that enters on the first bar a single
// window's squeeze releases; this one speaks only while the range is still
// dead. NOT atr_regime_halt: that pauses the book on the opposite tail, when
// volatility explodes; a dead range is not a hazard, so this observes instead.
// CALIBRATED ON: crypto majors, 1h bars. Both signals are percentile ranks of
// the instrument against itself, so the 90 and 3 thresholds travel; what does
// not travel is the 120-bar history length, which assumes a continuous 24-hour
// session - a session-bound instrument packs fewer regimes into 120 bars.
strategy DeadRangeStandaside {

    every 1h {

        if ATR_PCTL_INV(120) >= 90 and RANGE_QUIET_COUNT >= 3 {

            observe()

        }

    }

}
